          <msContents>
            <summary>Collection of medical, veterinary and other receipts, in German: including a transcript of the first nine chapters of Johann Binhard's 'Tröstlicher Haus-Spiegel'. Erfürt: 1621 [Receipts for children's diseases], and some incantations and magical remedies. The MS. is mainly in the hand of Werther Hoin, who names himself on the second line of fol. 60, and who seems to have been made 'Stalmeister' in the 'Freies Adelisches Kloster, Springirssbach'. On fol. 55v, and 56r he gives lists of the Monks there under their Abbot Johan Friedrich von Aubach, and of the laity who were in service at the Monastery. Under the date 1630 on fol 57v and 58r are notes on the purchase of a horse, and an agreement with a Courier. In other parts of the MS. are notes of events in Nassau 1626-31. (ff. 3, 4, 55.) The work by Binhard occupies ff. 26-32. The full title is 'Tröstlicher Hauss Spiegel: dass ist: Kurtzer doch warhafter Bericht, darinnen viertzig gewisse undt wohlbewehrte Experimenta undt Kunst-Stücke, fast fuhr alle Kranckheit der jungen Kinder zu finden ... Gedruckt zu Erfurdt bey Johann Röhbock. Anno Christi. M.DC. XXI'. Fl. 50-53r contain medical receipts by late 18th cent. hands. On the outside of the lower cover is a name 'Christoph Brüher [?]' with date 1653: but the letters are badly rubbed. In the lower margin of fol. 3 'Philippus Wehner. Anno Domini 1656'. On fol. 5 is the date 1745, on fol. 4v, 1784, and on fol. 54v, 1770.</summary>
